# Dependencies
node_modules/
# package-lock.json IS tracked: `npm ci` (used by .forgejo/workflows/ci.yml and
# by the release build) refuses to run without it, and OWASP A03 in
# RELEASE_CHECKLIST.md requires the lockfile to be committed with the release.

# Build outputs
js/
# translationfiles/ is tracked in full since the move to VoxCloud's own Weblate (2026-11):
# translationfiles/<lang>/introvox.po is the source of the translations and Weblate its only
# writer; the POT and l10n/*.js|json are derived by scripts/l10n-sync.mjs. Nothing here may be
# ignored, or Weblate's commits and the POT silently drop out of the repo.

# l10n/en.json + en.js are generated build artifacts (scripts/extract-en-json.js).
# Never commit them.
# NOTE: l10n/.source-count.json and l10n/.source-strings.json ARE committed on
# purpose — scripts/check-l10n-sync.js compares against them to catch source
# strings that never made it into the POT, and so never reached Weblate.
l10n/en.json
l10n/en.js
*.tar.gz
